trying to steal everything I got,

00:23:02.120 --> 00:23:02.953
I'm sitting here,

00:23:02.953 --> 00:23:04.050
I'm looking at his face,

00:23:04.050 --> 00:23:04.883
looking at him,

00:23:04.883 --> 00:23:05.716
I'm looking at the table,

00:23:05.716 --> 00:23:06.760
that pin up there.

00:23:06.760 --> 00:23:08.360
I want that damn pin.

00:23:08.360 --> 00:23:10.963
And as soon as he turns his
back I'm wanna take the pin.

00:23:12.140 --> 00:23:14.940
I'm talking to a lady
but she got a little,

00:23:14.940 --> 00:23:16.140
short dress on.

00:23:16.140 --> 00:23:17.700
I'm still looking at her in the eyes,

00:23:17.700 --> 00:23:19.350
I'm looking down between her legs.

00:23:19.350 --> 00:23:21.680
Yes ma'am, and we are
gonna take care of that

00:23:21.680 --> 00:23:23.350
and I'm gonna sign these papers,

00:23:23.350 --> 00:23:25.050
and why are you not looking at me?

00:23:26.260 --> 00:23:28.500
Why are you looking down?

00:23:28.500 --> 00:23:30.840
'Cause you looking at what you want.

00:23:30.840 --> 00:23:33.080
And all we gotta do is sit back

00:23:34.340 --> 00:23:37.630
and pay attention to everything
that goes on around us.

00:23:37.630 --> 00:23:39.810
And again, I'll say this here,

00:23:39.810 --> 00:23:41.710
when you hear me speak like this

00:23:43.040 --> 00:23:47.403
you say, this man never went
to school a day in his life.

00:23:48.440 --> 00:23:49.420
How do he learn,

00:23:49.420 --> 00:23:50.730
and again, no library,

00:23:50.730 --> 00:23:53.510
no phone, computer illiterate.

00:23:53.510 --> 00:23:56.840
So you say where did he get this knowledge

00:23:56.840 --> 00:23:57.933
to speak like that?

00:23:59.430 --> 00:24:00.947
Living in different cultures
and paying attention

00:24:00.947 --> 00:24:03.040
to what's going on around me.

00:24:03.040 --> 00:24:05.800
My point is you don't need,

00:24:05.800 --> 00:24:08.390
you would want society to
teach you certain things

00:24:08.390 --> 00:24:11.610
and we do need to learn
certain things out of society,

00:24:11.610 --> 00:24:13.410
but if you give yourself a chance,

00:24:13.410 --> 00:24:16.140
you don't need people
to teach you anything

00:24:16.140 --> 00:24:18.910
if you stay focused and
pay attention around you

00:24:18.910 --> 00:24:21.873
and read the signs of stores, read signs.

00:24:22.910 --> 00:24:25.137
Look at a book and then find
out what that story really

00:24:25.137 --> 00:24:26.190
has to give you?

00:24:26.190 --> 00:24:27.870
Find out what this Bible,

00:24:27.870 --> 00:24:30.177
what that book you're reading
really have to give you?

00:24:30.177 --> 00:24:33.940
And if you read it and then you
go out and you pay attention

00:24:33.940 --> 00:24:35.907
to every single thing or you just look,

00:24:35.907 --> 00:24:37.000
you're just looking,

00:24:37.000 --> 00:24:38.310
walking around and looking,

00:24:38.310 --> 00:24:40.660
but you pay attention to
all things around you.

00:24:41.660 --> 00:24:43.843
Like these high tech cameras here,

00:24:43.843 --> 00:24:45.863
I never touched one in my life,

00:24:46.970 --> 00:24:50.530
but I guarantee you if you
set one down in front of me

00:24:50.530 --> 00:24:53.220
on a stand like that and
I took a look over it,

00:24:53.220 --> 00:24:55.920
it might take me a couple of hours,

00:24:55.920 --> 00:24:57.990
but I believe I'd be able to work

00:24:57.990 --> 00:25:00.920
that thing like a National
Geographic photographer

00:25:00.920 --> 00:25:04.130
if I just gave myself a chance, see.

00:25:04.130 --> 00:25:06.720
Because we can do
anything we choose to do,

00:25:06.720 --> 00:25:08.270
and that don't mean financially.

00:25:08.270 --> 00:25:09.650
People say, we can do anything,

00:25:09.650 --> 00:25:11.100
but that don't mean you gonna get up

00:25:11.100 --> 00:25:12.350
and go make $100 million.

00:25:13.287 --> 00:25:15.640
But that mean you can get your mind right.

00:25:15.640 --> 00:25:17.200
You know, not genuine,

00:25:17.200 --> 00:25:19.185
but I watched the "Star Wars" picture.

00:25:19.185 --> 00:25:20.590
"Star Wars" is one of my favorite.

00:25:20.590 --> 00:25:23.260
And I asked a guy, I say,

00:25:23.260 --> 00:25:25.150
for two cigarettes now you let me see

00:25:25.150 --> 00:25:26.460
how good you know your movies.

00:25:26.460 --> 00:25:28.900
I say, what did Yoda say to Obi-Wan Kenobi

00:25:28.900 --> 00:25:30.770
in the swamps about Luke Skywalker?

00:25:30.770 --> 00:25:31.973
Well, I don't know.

00:25:33.380 --> 00:25:34.310
I told him, I said,

00:25:34.310 --> 00:25:36.670
Yoda said this to Obi-Wan Kenobi.

00:25:36.670 --> 00:25:37.503
Now, listen to this.

00:25:37.503 --> 00:25:38.577
This is years ago.

00:25:38.577 --> 00:25:40.090
I know you think that it's just a movie

00:25:40.090 --> 00:25:41.250
but his is what Obi-Wan,

00:25:41.250 --> 00:25:42.600
Yoda said to Obi-Wan Kenobi.

00:25:42.600 --> 00:25:44.563
And you said, how did he remember that?

00:25:45.440 --> 00:25:48.090
All these years later he remembered that.

00:25:48.090 --> 00:25:49.640
Yoda

00:25:49.640 --> 00:25:52.250
told Obi-Wan Kenobi in the swamp

00:25:52.250 --> 00:25:54.240
about Luke Skywalker when
he was young and wild.

00:25:54.240 --> 00:25:56.050
He said, the boy cannot learn.

00:25:56.050 --> 00:25:57.743
He has no discipline.

00:25:58.600 --> 00:26:00.380
And Yoda asked him and said,

00:26:00.380 --> 00:26:02.773
was I any different when you taught me?

00:26:04.380 --> 00:26:05.250
And Yoda

00:26:06.239 --> 00:26:08.633
got the message which means,

00:26:10.120 --> 00:26:13.000
the student taught the
teacher something, see.

00:26:14.610 --> 00:26:16.093
Yoda was the master.

00:26:17.390 --> 00:26:20.540
He had given up 'cause
he got up in his old age.

00:26:20.540 --> 00:26:22.720
He was about to give up on Luke Skywalker.

00:26:22.720 --> 00:26:25.820
The boy cannot learn 'cause
he has no discipline.

00:26:25.820 --> 00:26:28.963
But was I any different
when you taught me?

00:26:29.930 --> 00:26:33.420
And Yoda looked up and
did not have an answer

00:26:34.710 --> 00:26:38.410
which means the student
that he taught came back

00:26:38.410 --> 00:26:41.000
and delivered something to the teacher

00:26:41.000 --> 00:26:42.193
and taught the teacher.

00:26:44.330 --> 00:26:48.170
Which means anybody can do
anything and will learn.

00:26:48.170 --> 00:26:49.003
And that's another thing,

00:26:49.003 --> 00:26:50.390
we read books,

00:26:50.390 --> 00:26:52.103
we look at movies.

00:26:52.980 --> 00:26:55.450
We don't understand what the intelligence

00:26:55.450 --> 00:26:57.370
of the movie giving gus.

00:26:57.370 --> 00:26:58.580
If you looked at "Star Wars",

00:26:58.580 --> 00:27:01.500
the power of the dark
side and the Jedi Knight,

00:27:01.500 --> 00:27:06.420
that was heaven and hell
fighting against each other.

00:27:06.420 --> 00:27:07.887
That's why they kept saying,

00:27:07.887 --> 00:27:10.017
"The power of the dark side."

00:27:10.970 --> 00:27:13.500
The emperor was Lucifer coming in.

00:27:13.500 --> 00:27:15.737
Luke Skywalker was the angel that God sent

00:27:17.220 --> 00:27:19.283
to defeat Lucifer.

00:27:20.360 --> 00:27:23.350
So everything's about life,

00:27:23.350 --> 00:27:27.053
even the movies that
you see is about life.

00:27:28.260 --> 00:27:29.830
The bank robbery in the movie, "Heat",

00:27:29.830 --> 00:27:31.910
Downtown Los Angeles.

00:27:31.910 --> 00:27:34.790
Robert De Niro and Al
Pacino shooting it out

00:27:36.070 --> 00:27:38.910
in the middle of Los Angeles streets.

00:27:38.910 --> 00:27:40.960
Remember that thing long
time ago in North Hollywood

00:27:40.960 --> 00:27:42.475
where that bank robbery
where they were shooting out

00:27:42.475 --> 00:27:43.925
in the middle of the streets?

00:27:44.840 --> 00:27:46.900
You didn't get that message
when they killed them two boys

00:27:46.900 --> 00:27:48.600
out there in North Hollywood.

00:27:48.600 --> 00:27:49.433
They was robbing that bank

00:27:49.433 --> 00:27:50.407
and then they come with the movie,

00:27:50.407 --> 00:27:52.160
"Heat" years later.

00:27:52.160 --> 00:27:53.290
But it was Downtown.

00:27:53.290 --> 00:27:55.700
They had to change the
scenario a little bit,

00:27:55.700 --> 00:27:57.830
but it was Downtown Los Angeles.

00:27:57.830 --> 00:28:00.777
And this was a real life thing

00:28:00.777 --> 00:28:02.400
but most people didn't get that.

00:28:02.400 --> 00:28:04.773
That was the bank robbery in Burbank,

00:28:06.560 --> 00:28:07.860
yeah, in Burbank about 10,

00:28:08.850 --> 00:28:11.320
20 years ago when they
killed them two boys

00:28:11.320 --> 00:28:14.230
and them guys had the machine
guns robbing that bank,

00:28:14.230 --> 00:28:15.530
then years later came with "Heat".

00:28:15.530 --> 00:28:17.323
So my point is this, people,

00:28:18.290 --> 00:28:19.983
everything pertains to life.

00:28:21.127 --> 00:28:23.037
"Ain't no need to worry

00:28:23.037 --> 00:28:25.187
"'cause it'll be all
over in thee morning."

00:28:26.780 --> 00:28:27.767
And there's another one,

00:28:27.767 --> 00:28:29.087
"Baby don't worry,

00:28:29.087 --> 00:28:31.437
"Everything little thing's
gonna be all right."

00:28:32.740 --> 00:28:35.480
One more, ain't got nowhere to live.

00:28:35.480 --> 00:28:37.470
Cigarette Man, ain't got no money.

00:28:37.470 --> 00:28:38.470
Ain't got no wife,

00:28:38.470 --> 00:28:40.317
ain't got no family.

00:28:40.317 --> 00:28:43.560
"But don't worry, be happy."

00:28:43.560 --> 00:28:46.930
That's all we can do 'cause
we cannot control the things

00:28:46.930 --> 00:28:48.823
we wanna control on this planet.

00:28:50.170 --> 00:28:52.153
No one man can control that.

00:28:52.153 --> 00:28:54.030
I don't know one female.

00:28:54.030 --> 00:28:57.980
We do the best we can in life
and that's all that we do

00:28:57.980 --> 00:28:59.470
and then we move on.

00:28:59.470 --> 00:29:01.630
And nobody's character's the same.

00:29:01.630 --> 00:29:03.270
We've had presidents,

00:29:03.270 --> 00:29:05.368
everybody from all the '60s.

00:29:05.368 --> 00:29:08.090
Jesus Christ was the first assassination

00:29:08.090 --> 00:29:09.300
when they hung him on the cross.

00:29:09.300 --> 00:29:11.470
Abraham Lincoln freed the blacks,

00:29:11.470 --> 00:29:14.380
they hated him and shot him
in the back of the head.

00:29:14.380 --> 00:29:16.230
John F. Kennedy and Robert F. Kennedy,

00:29:16.230 --> 00:29:18.990
two brothers were very
noble but they died.

00:29:18.990 --> 00:29:22.120
Malcolm X wanted to
stand up for the brothers

00:29:22.120 --> 00:29:23.190
'cause they felt like,

00:29:23.190 --> 00:29:24.870
and some of the things he said was right

00:29:24.870 --> 00:29:26.710
and some of the things he said was wrong,

00:29:26.710 --> 00:29:29.400
because he felt like we
wasn't getting a fair hand.

00:29:29.400 --> 00:29:30.470
They killed him.

00:29:30.470 --> 00:29:32.990
Martin Luther King wanted to
do it a little bit different.

00:29:32.990 --> 00:29:34.530
He wanted to go for all the people,

00:29:34.530 --> 00:29:35.510
which is a noble thing.

00:29:35.510 --> 00:29:38.190
Both men were noble but he wanted

00:29:38.190 --> 00:29:39.520
to help the people, period,

00:29:39.520 --> 00:29:40.703
but they killed him.

00:29:43.530 --> 00:29:45.760
And can't no one person control the world

00:29:47.890 --> 00:29:49.310
and if you try

00:29:51.120 --> 00:29:52.383
they'll kill you too.

00:29:54.910 --> 00:29:57.940
So what my point is, people,

00:29:57.940 --> 00:29:59.033
try to live.

00:30:00.070 --> 00:30:01.103
Try to be happy.

00:30:01.970 --> 00:30:03.910
You got YouTube, you got Facebook,

00:30:03.910 --> 00:30:06.140
you got all kinds of things you could do.

00:30:06.140 --> 00:30:07.273
You got business.

00:30:08.350 --> 00:30:09.890
If you don't wanna do nothing else.

00:30:09.890 --> 00:30:10.860
Do you know,

00:30:10.860 --> 00:30:13.170
I don't know if I told you
this in my first interview,

00:30:13.170 --> 00:30:16.230
but do you know about
25 years ago I wanted

00:30:16.230 --> 00:30:17.370
to leave Los Angeles.

00:30:17.370 --> 00:30:20.170
About 30 years ago I wanted
to leave Los Angeles so bad.

00:30:21.410 --> 00:30:22.287
And I didn't have the money

00:30:22.287 --> 00:30:24.470
and one night I walked out
the door and I told my buddy,

00:30:24.470 --> 00:30:25.760
I said, I'm leaving in the morning.

00:30:25.760 --> 00:30:27.900
He said, well where you going?

00:30:27.900 --> 00:30:29.630
How you gonna leave?

00:30:29.630 --> 00:30:32.060
I said, I'm gonna take that 10-speed Huffy

00:30:32.060 --> 00:30:33.760
and I'm gonna ride that
all the way down 10

00:30:33.760 --> 00:30:35.420
to Fort Lauderdale, Florida.

00:30:35.420 --> 00:30:37.030
And I did that.

00:30:37.030 --> 00:30:38.763
The next morning I got up.

00:30:39.925 --> 00:30:42.320
I brought my bike downstairs.

00:30:42.320 --> 00:30:46.120
It was on San Julian and 5th Street.

00:30:46.120 --> 00:30:47.367
And I got on that 10-speed Huffy.

00:30:47.367 --> 00:30:48.900
I left a house full of furniture.

00:30:48.900 --> 00:30:50.657
I was in the SRO.

00:30:50.657 --> 00:30:52.880
I left a house full of
furniture in there and money

00:30:52.880 --> 00:30:55.270
and I'd got on Highway 10
which started over here.

00:30:55.270 --> 00:30:56.790
They tell me it started in Santa Monica,

00:30:56.790 --> 00:30:58.680
but I thought it started over here just

00:30:58.680 --> 00:31:00.510
on the other side of Downtown.

00:31:00.510 --> 00:31:03.080
But somebody told me now
that 10 runs all the way down

00:31:03.080 --> 00:31:05.250
to Santa Monica but I
didn't start from there.

00:31:05.250 --> 00:31:06.670
I started from over here so I thought

00:31:06.670 --> 00:31:08.320
that's where 10 started at.

00:31:08.320 --> 00:31:09.670
But I took 10

00:31:10.860 --> 00:31:13.083
all the way down to the bottom of Florida.

00:31:13.083 --> 00:31:15.520
So I got almost to Fort Worden Beach

00:31:15.520 --> 00:31:17.840
and I had two flat tires.

00:31:17.840 --> 00:31:21.913
And the guy put the bike
on the back of his truck,

00:31:23.928 --> 00:31:26.260
he drove me over to his house

00:31:26.260 --> 00:31:27.730
and the front fork was broke.

00:31:27.730 --> 00:31:29.057
But do you know what this man told me

00:31:29.057 --> 00:31:31.157
when he found out where I was coming from?

00:31:32.020 --> 00:31:35.120
He said, I'll give you $200 for that bike

00:31:35.120 --> 00:31:37.420
and take you to Fort Lauderdale.

00:31:37.420 --> 00:31:39.360
I said, but the bike is toe up, sir.

00:31:39.360 --> 00:31:41.070
To buy new forks for that
bike you'd would have

00:31:41.070 --> 00:31:42.740
to buy a whole new bike.

00:31:42.740 --> 00:31:44.560
You just can't buy new forks for the bike

00:31:44.560 --> 00:31:46.560
'cause the bike is split with the forks.

00:31:47.540 --> 00:31:50.510
He said, I don't care what
you say about that bike,

00:31:50.510 --> 00:31:51.387
that bike got a lot of history

00:31:51.387 --> 00:31:54.650
and I'll give you $200 and buy
you a ticket for that bike.

00:31:54.650 --> 00:31:55.823
And he did.

00:31:57.000 --> 00:32:00.050
I never saw him again but he
was a good man, white guy.

00:32:00.050 --> 00:32:02.030
He was a damn good man.

00:32:02.030 --> 00:32:03.270
And when I left that night,

00:32:03.270 --> 00:32:04.430
I mean, the next day,

00:32:04.430 --> 00:32:06.080
he shook my hand.

00:32:06.080 --> 00:32:08.137
I knew then this would be
the one and only time me

00:32:08.137 --> 00:32:10.250
and this guy would meet.

00:32:10.250 --> 00:32:11.870
But he fed me and took me in his house

00:32:11.870 --> 00:32:13.750
and didn't know me from Adam.

00:32:13.750 --> 00:32:16.330
I could've been a killer
coming across that highway.

00:32:16.330 --> 00:32:19.370
I could've been a ruthless person.

00:32:19.370 --> 00:32:21.083
He did not even know.

00:32:21.930 --> 00:32:24.120
But he opened his house
to me and then he went in

00:32:24.120 --> 00:32:27.270
and laid down in his
bed and closed his eyes

00:32:27.270 --> 00:32:29.950
and had a good night's sleep on a man he

00:32:29.950 --> 00:32:31.460
had never met in his life,

00:32:31.460 --> 00:32:32.510
a black man.

00:32:32.510 --> 00:32:35.630
Not that the color would
matter but I'm just saying,

00:32:35.630 --> 00:32:39.200
I threw that in there because
back then there was a lot

00:32:39.200 --> 00:32:42.070
of animosity between
different races, Spanish,

00:32:42.070 --> 00:32:43.017
blacks and whites.

00:32:43.017 --> 00:32:44.190
There was a lot of animosity.

00:32:44.190 --> 00:32:46.467
And this happened at a
time when the animosity

00:32:46.467 --> 00:32:48.663
and the stress level was great.

00:32:50.730 --> 00:32:53.440
So this was years ago.

00:32:53.440 --> 00:32:55.710
So for him to do that

00:32:55.710 --> 00:32:58.060
to me was a very noble thing

00:32:59.640 --> 00:33:02.140
because he didn't know me from Adam.

00:33:02.140 --> 00:33:04.386
And I could've woke up that
night and did anything,

00:33:04.386 --> 00:33:05.352
set his house on fire,

00:33:05.352 --> 00:33:07.350
killed him, anything.

00:33:07.350 --> 00:33:09.610
But I made $200 and I have
made a little money all the way

00:33:09.610 --> 00:33:10.560
down the highway.

00:33:10.560 --> 00:33:14.923
But my point was I rode
that 10-speed down there,

00:33:15.778 --> 00:33:16.611
oh, by the way,

00:33:16.611 --> 00:33:18.170
there was two cops that told me,

00:33:18.170 --> 00:33:20.250
two highway patrols told
me I couldn't ride the bike

00:33:20.250 --> 00:33:21.200
on the highway.

00:33:21.200 --> 00:33:23.640
But once they found out
where I was riding from,

00:33:23.640 --> 00:33:25.140
do you know these two people,

00:33:25.140 --> 00:33:26.900
these two officers gave me a free pass,

00:33:26.900 --> 00:33:28.730
not at the same time,

00:33:28.730 --> 00:33:30.770
one in Arizona and one in Florida,

00:33:30.770 --> 00:33:33.045
and they gave me a free pass.

00:33:33.045 --> 00:33:35.670
And there wasn't nobody handing me water,

00:33:35.670 --> 00:33:37.070
wasn't no TV thing,

00:33:37.070 --> 00:33:38.710
wasn't no publicity stunt,

00:33:38.710 --> 00:33:39.753
I just did it.

00:33:41.250 --> 00:33:42.830
And so

00:33:42.830 --> 00:33:47.003
my point is if we dig deep inside us,

00:33:47.850 --> 00:33:49.703
if we dig real deep,

00:33:50.950 --> 00:33:53.560
there's something deep inside you

00:33:53.560 --> 00:33:54.933
that's waiting to come out.

00:33:56.350 --> 00:33:57.633
You gotta wake it up.

00:33:58.490 --> 00:34:00.183
You gotta bring it up out of you.

00:34:01.840 --> 00:34:02.893
It's in there.

00:34:03.860 --> 00:34:07.490
But if you think it's not and
you let people put you down

00:34:07.490 --> 00:34:09.810
or make you feel worthless,

00:34:09.810 --> 00:34:11.900
you will never find it.

